gve: Enable hw-gro by default if device supported

jira KERNEL-1712
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-6.12.0-211.62.1.el10_2
commit-author Ankit Garg <nktgrg@google.com>
commit 3c398063ef01b02d7efd31662154fe70fd28ace6
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-6.12.0-211.62.1.el10_2/3c398063.failed

Change the driver's default behavior to enable hw-gro whenever supported
for device.

Performance observations:
- We observed ~10% improvement in RX single stream throughput across
  various MTU sizes.
- No change in TCP_RR/TCP_CRR latencies

	Signed-off-by: Ankit Garg <nktgrg@google.com>
	Reviewed-by: Willem de Bruijn <willemb@google.com>
	Reviewed-by: Harshitha Ramamurthy <hramamurthy@google.com>
	Signed-off-by: Joshua Washington <joshwash@google.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260303195549.2679070-5-joshwash@google.com
	Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3c398063ef01b02d7efd31662154fe70fd28ace6)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/net/ethernet/google/gve/gve_adminq.c
diff --cc drivers/net/ethernet/google/gve/gve_adminq.c
index 002d5c1db1a8,129f3e11a442..000000000000
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/google/gve/gve_adminq.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/google/gve/gve_adminq.c
@@@ -1127,9 -1117,11 +1127,17 @@@ int gve_adminq_describe_device(struct g
  
  	gve_set_default_rss_sizes(priv);
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	/* DQO supports LRO. */
 +	if (!gve_is_gqi(priv))
 +		priv->dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_LRO;
++=======
+ 	/* DQO supports HW-GRO. */
+ 	if (gve_is_dqo(priv)) {
+ 		priv->dev->hw_features |= NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
+ 		priv->dev->features |= NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
+ 	}
++>>>>>>> 3c398063ef01 (gve: Enable hw-gro by default if device supported)
  
  	priv->max_registered_pages =
  				be64_to_cpu(descriptor->max_registered_pages);
* Unmerged path drivers/net/ethernet/google/gve/gve_adminq.c
